  answer: "Alabama's senior population is growing faster than the national average, and Birmingham's UAB medical district anchors one of the Southeast's largest health systems — a natural feeder for assisted living and memory care development across the Birmingham–Hoover metro and the Gulf Coast retirement corridor around Mobile and Baldwin County. Alabama enforces the IBC with state amendments; assisted living falls under residential board-and-care provisions while nursing facilities face health-care occupancy rules. Summer heat and humidity drive cooling-dominated MEP design, and Gulf Coast projects add wind-borne-debris and flood-zone detailing. Alabama operates a certificate-of-need program that applies to nursing facility beds, so project teams confirm CON status early.",
