  answer: "California holds the nation's largest senior population by far, and its residential care facilities for the elderly span everything from six-bed homes to large urban assisted living towers. Los Angeles, the Bay Area, San Diego, and Sacramento each carry deep waiting-list pressure for quality memory care. California licenses assisted living as residential care facilities for the elderly through the Department of Social Services — a social-services model, not a health-department one. Title 24 energy compliance, OSHPD-adjacent considerations for higher-acuity projects, and seismic detailing shape every senior project. California has no certificate-of-need program.",
  directAnswer: "Senior living development in California is licensed by the California Department of Social Services, and its engineering is shaped by california licenses assisted living as residential care facilities for the elderly through the Department of Social Services — a social-services model, not a health-department one. Apex Grid Engineering designs the full continuum — independent living, assisted living, memory care, and nursing — with MEP, structural, and civil engineering coordinated for California, plus fast entitlements support for developers racing demographic demand.",
