    { heading: "Little Rock senior housing market", body: "Little Rock state capital and the central Arkansas hospital hub. Northwest Arkansas's growth around Bentonville and Fayetteville is pulling senior housing investment into a market that historically built little of it, while Little Rock's hospital base supports assisted living and nursing demand across central Arkansas. The state's 65-plus share keeps climbing as younger residents leave rural counties. For developers, the Little Rock market rewards projects that match the local demand profile — the care levels, price points, and amenity expectations of the households actually moving here — rather than a national template." },
    { heading: "Engineering senior living in Little Rock", body: "Arkansas licenses assisted living at Level I and Level II through the Department of Human Services, with higher-acuity memory care pushing projects toward stricter life-safety detailing. Tornado and severe-weather hardening, plus humid summers, shape structural and MEP scope. Certificate-of-need applies to nursing facility beds in Arkansas. In Little Rock specifically, that means a mechanical basis of design tuned to local conditions, electrical with emergency and standby architecture for a non-evacuating population, plumbing designed around senior-safe bathrooms and reliable hot water, and life safety under the correct NFPA 101 occupancy chapter — confirmed with the AHJ before design development." },
    { heading: "Getting a Little Rock project permitted", body: "The Little Rock entitlement path runs through the local building department's plan check plus the Arkansas Department of Human Services's physical-plant review — two tracks, two checklists, best engaged in parallel. Early pre-submittal meetings that confirm occupancy classification, sprinkler standard, and submittal requirements compress the timeline more than any drafting acceleration. Apex Grid's senior living practice is built for exactly this: front-loaded decisions, coordinated disciplines, fewer correction cycles." }
